  "qualified_behaviors": [
    "Canonical immutable .pprov records distinguish origins and notices without changing cooked asset identity.",
    "Preview, stale guards, exact retry, undo/redo and failed mixed transactions preserve authored atomicity.",
    "Metadata pagination does not read record files; dependency freeze freshly checks all selected records, including unused asset mappings.",
    "Unused cooked assets are excluded from closure; all selected provenance records and deterministic credits are retained.",
    "Saved frozen mapping A is validated on active and fresh-owner restoration after current authoring changes to B.",
    "Correctly hashed forged cooked-kind records, corrupt/missing records, symlinks and malformed UTF-8/duplicate keys reject.",
    "Relocated metadata-only bundles preserve records and credits; refreshed inventories cannot legitimize contradictory credits or invalid record content.",
    "Legacy worlds and bundles with no mappings retain their original shape and do not gain provenance payloads."
  ],
